---
id: org.dxos.plugin.thread
name: ThreadPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

ThreadPlugin provides chat: channels backed by an ECHO feed and free-standing message threads.
It renders the channel article + companion surfaces and a thread surface, and contributes the
operations that create a channel and append messages. Shared message/thread UI comes from
`@dxos/react-ui-thread`, and the `Channel`/`Message`/`Thread` schema comes from `@dxos/types`.
Document comments and the comment-thread AI agent live in `@dxos/plugin-comments`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Channel
  desc: |
    A chat channel. Defined in @dxos/types. Carries an optional `feed` Ref whose
    queue holds the channel's Message objects in order.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op OnCreateSpace
  key: org.dxos.plugin.thread.operation.onCreateSpace
  desc: On space creation, create a default "General" channel in the root collection.
```

```mdl
op CreateChannel
  key: org.dxos.operation.thread.createChannel
  desc: Create a new Channel in the given space.
  in:
    spaceId: SpaceId
    name?: String
  out:
    object: Channel
```

```mdl
op AppendChannelMessage
  key: org.dxos.operation.thread.appendChannelMessage
  desc: Append a Message authored by `sender` to the channel's feed.
  in:
    channel: Channel
    sender: Actor
    text: String
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Channel chat
  req F-1.1: A Channel article MUST render its feed messages newest-last with a
    pinned composer; sending invokes AppendChannelMessage.
  req F-1.2: Externally-synced channels (those carrying foreign-key Obj.Meta) MUST
    render read-only — the composer is suppressed.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Thread chat
  req F-2.1: A Thread article MUST render the thread's messages and append new
    messages by pushing onto `thread.messages`.
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create a channel and send a message
  desc: The core thread round-trip — create a Channel, send a message, read it back from the feed.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - identityDid: an identity exists, its DID used as the message `sender`
    - space: a space is open
    - no Channel named "QA Channel" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the channel
      do: In the navtree, click + on the space and choose Channel. Name it "QA Channel".
      invoke: [op:CreateChannel] { spaceId: $given.space.id, name: "QA Channel" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Channel named "QA Channel" now exists and opens in the channel article
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the space
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.space }
      expect: "QA Channel" appears as a row in the navtree
    - name: Send a message
      do: In the composer at the bottom of the channel article, type "Hello QA" and press Enter.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.thread.appendChannelMessage {
          channel: $created.object,
          sender: { identityDid: $given.identityDid },
          text: "Hello QA"
        }
      expect: "Hello QA" appears as the newest (bottom-most) message in the feed
      note: |
        `output: void` — Rule 3 applies: verify the effect, not the return value. Reading the
        feed's queue is not expressible as a synchronous DOM/db snippet here, so this step is
        judged by `expect` alone.
  after:
    - name: Delete the channel
      do: Right-click "QA Channel" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.space }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Default "General" channel on space creation
  desc: The lifecycle hook that seeds every new space with a channel — no user gesture involved.
  actors: agent
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
  test:
    - name: Create a new space
      do: Click "Create space" (or invoke the equivalent action).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.create {}
      capture: created
      expect: a new space is created
      assert: return !!$created.space
    - name: Confirm the default channel exists
      do: Open the new space's navtree and look for a "General" channel.
      expect: a Channel named "General" exists in the root collection of the new space
      note: |
        NO separate `invoke` — `org.dxos.plugin.thread.operation.onCreateSpace` is a lifecycle
        hook the space-creation pipeline runs itself, not something this flow calls directly; this
        step only verifies the effect.
      assert: |
        return (await $created.space.db.query(dxos.Filter.type(Channel)).run())
          .objects.some((c) => c.name === 'General');
  after:
    - name: Delete the space
      do: Right-click the new space in the navtree and choose Delete space.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.delete { space: $created.space }
      expect: the space leaves the navtree
```
